From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:35:09 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: cpufeature: hide WFxT on Apple M4+ without a
 forced override

Apple M4 and later cores have WFxT hidden by injecting
"id_aa64isar2.wfxt=0" into the early ID register override after the
boot arguments are parsed. The override mechanism exists for boot
arguments, so init_cpu_ftr_reg() reports it at warning level on every
boot:

  CPU features: SYS_ID_AA64ISAR2_EL1[3:0]: forced to 0

Clear the WFxT field when each CPU's ID registers are recorded instead.
The sanitised ID_AA64ISAR2_EL1 still reads WFxT as absent, so
ARM64_HAS_WFXT stays off, KVM guests do not see it and HWCAP2_WFXT is
not set. A boot argument still cannot re-enable it:
"id_aa64isar2.wfxt=1" is above the lower safe value and is ignored.

Nothing used the override before the boot CPU records its ID registers:
__delay() only takes the WFxT path once ARM64_HAS_WFXT is finalised.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c           | 9 +++++++++
 arch/arm64/kernel/pi/idreg-override.c | 8 --------
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c
index 47f8b5837a..006cec6958 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpuinfo.c
@@ -549,6 +549,15 @@ static void __cpuinfo_store_cpu(struct cpuinfo_arm64 *info)
 	info->reg_id_aa64isar0 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64ISAR0_EL1);
 	info->reg_id_aa64isar1 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64ISAR1_EL1);
 	info->reg_id_aa64isar2 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64ISAR2_EL1);
+	/*
+	 * Timed waits bypass the register-saving idle path on Apple M4 and
+	 * later cores. Record WFxT as absent on every CPU, so the sanitised
+	 * register hides it from the kernel, KVM guests and userspace
+	 * (HWCAP2_WFXT) and a boot argument cannot bring it back.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) &&
+	    midr_is_apple_m4_or_later(info->reg_midr))
+		info->reg_id_aa64isar2 &= ~ID_AA64ISAR2_EL1_WFxT;
 	info->reg_id_aa64isar3 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64ISAR3_EL1);
 	info->reg_id_aa64mmfr0 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64MMFR0_EL1);
 	info->reg_id_aa64mmfr1 = read_cpuid(ID_AA64MMFR1_EL1);
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/pi/idreg-override.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/pi/idreg-override.c
index 63e29ca569..8c008deda6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/pi/idreg-override.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/pi/idreg-override.c
@@ -12,7 +12,6 @@
 
 #include <asm/cacheflush.h>
 #include <asm/cpufeature.h>
-#include <asm/cputype.h>
 #include <asm/setup.h>
 
 #include "pi.h"
@@ -458,13 +457,6 @@ void __init init_feature_override(u64 boot_status, const void *fdt,
 
 	parse_cmdline(fdt, chosen);
 
-	/*
-	 * Timed waits bypass the register-saving idle path on Apple M4+ cores.
-	 * Apply this after boot arguments so they cannot re-enable WFxT.
-	 */
-	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) && midr_is_apple_m4_or_later(read_cpuid_id()))
-		__parse_cmdline("id_aa64isar2.wfxt=0", false);
-
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(regs); i++) {
 		reg = prel64_pointer(regs[i].reg);
 		override = prel64_pointer(reg->override);
